    <item>
      <title>v0.3</title>
      <link>https://css.techhive.net/changelog</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">css-showcase-v0.3</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><strong>October 23, 2026</strong></p><h3>New</h3><ul><li>A warmer color identity: the whole site now wears the Manila Sunrise palette — ivory light mode, deep olive-black dark mode, and terracotta accents throughout.</li><li>Eight new form demos: number steppers, color pickers, autocomplete comboboxes, fieldsets, meters, live output fields, time pickers, and one-time-code inputs — the native HTML controls, styled properly.</li><li>A shareable image for every demo: download or copy a 1:1 snapshot with the live preview, title, and CSS features for social posts and docs.</li><li>Search everything with a ⌘K command palette, and demo links that remember the exact device and pattern you picked.</li></ul><h3>Fixed</h3><ul><li>Mobile visitors can now open the navigation menu — the menu button used to be missing on small screens.</li><li>Dark mode now applies before the first paint (no more light flash) and follows your system setting until you pick a theme.</li><li>Copy buttons confirm with a toast instead of failing quietly.</li><li>Every demo switcher is fully keyboard-operable with arrow keys.</li><li>On phones, the floating button cluster no longer covers page headers, and dense demo content like verification codes and time fields now fits inside the phone frame.</li><li>The site now sends standard security headers on every page.</li></ul><h3>Improved</h3><ul><li>The library grows to 44 demos.</li><li>A large internal cleanup removed around two thousand lines of duplicated code.</li><li>Developer documentation was refreshed so contributors can get started faster.</li></ul>]]></description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>v0.2</title>
      <link>https://css.techhive.net/changelog</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">css-showcase-v0.2</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><strong>September 13, 2026</strong></p><h3>New</h3><ul><li>A new name and look: the site is now CSS Showcase, with our own logo, matching icons, and rich previews when a page is shared.</li><li>A "Send to LLM" button that copies ready-made instructions, so an AI assistant can rebuild any demo inside your own project.</li><li>A playful not-found page built from pure CSS, complete with a spinning zero, floating CSS properties, and a free lesson in centering things.</li><li>Plain-language legal pages: Terms, Privacy, DMCA, Cookies, Disclaimer, and User Content, all linked in the footer.</li><li>This changelog page, plus an RSS feed you can subscribe to and follow along.</li><li>Quick access to our GitHub from the top corner, and a spot in the footer highlighting our other projects.</li></ul><h3>Fixed</h3><ul><li>Live reload now works properly: pages update instantly while being edited instead of needing a restart.</li><li>The line above the page content and the line under the sidebar header now sit at exactly the same height.</li><li>The command for previewing the finished site locally works again.</li><li>Removed the duplicate site name that used to appear twice at the top of the page.</li></ul><h3>Improved</h3><ul><li>A deep clean for open source: internal tooling was removed and automated quality checks now run on every change.</li><li>Better directions for search engines and social networks, including our official web address.</li><li>A plain-text guide so AI assistants can understand the site and its content.</li><li>One-command deployment on Cloudflare Pages.</li></ul>]]></description>
    </item>
